## Main-file resolution

{% raw %}A **root** is a `.tex` file with `\documentclass` at the start of a line. Resolution prefers a root
{% endraw %}
named `main.tex`, then a root named `paper.tex`, then the single root; a dir with several roots and
no `main.tex`/`paper.tex` is flagged with an empty `main_tex`, never guessed. Outcomes:
{{ p['main-file outcomes'] }}

The name test is applied to roots, not to files, {{ p['main.tex without documentclass'] }}
{% raw %}declare no `\documentclass` — companion and build copies — so a bare-name preference would pick a
{% endraw %}
non-root file.

